  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This CaltechDATA dataset currently shows one documented downstream reuse, through its associated article. Beyond that, the record is still early: OpenAlex lists no citations yet, DataCite reports no recorded views or downloads, and there is no captured public discussion in the available archive.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The clearest impact signal for this dataset is reuse rather than broad dissemination. It is linked to a single associated article, indicating that the data have already supported a scholarly publication and have entered an explicit reuse pathway. That makes the dataset more than a passive deposit: it has functioned as source material for subsequent analysis.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At the same time, the surrounding metrics suggest a modest and still-developing visibility profile. OpenAlex does not yet record citations to the dataset, and the available DataCite record shows no views or downloads. Those zeros should be read as a snapshot of the current record, not as a statement about eventual influence.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The subject matter and metadata point to a computational biology context, with emphasis on package selection, software versioning, and single-cell RNA-seq analysis. The dataset is openly accessible through CaltechDATA and is linked as a supplement to the associated article, which helps anchor it within a reproducible research workflow.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the evidence supports an early-stage impact story centered on scholarly reuse. The dataset has already contributed to a related publication, but the citation and usage record remains sparse, so its longer-term reach has not yet been established in the available sources.</p>",
